<h3>Key Challenges Ahead</h3>
<p>Despite the benefits, the paper outlines critical bottlenecks before latent space becomes the native substrate for next-generation intelligence:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Interpretability:</strong> Since computations happen in continuous vector coordinate space, debugging why a model arrived at a conclusion is highly challenging.</li>
  <li><strong>Controllability:</strong> Direct post-hoc intervention on latent states is more complex than simple text-level prompting or token editing.</li>
  <li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Testing intermediate reasoning steps requires projection heads or specialized probe classifiers.</li>
</ol>
</section>

